  chapter: "Chapter 1: Ryōmen Sukuna’s Trap",
  story: "Yuji Itadori is a cheerful first‑year high‑school student blessed with unbelievable physical strength. He turns down every sports‑club invitation, choosing instead to join the school’s Occult Research Club with classmates Sasaki and Iguchi.<br><br>A young jujutsu sorcerer named Megumi Fushiguro arrives at the school searching for a special cursed‑object: one of the twenty fingers belonging to Ryōmen Sukuna, the brutal ancient King of Curses. He learns the club has the finger stored, still sealed.<br><br>Before the evening comes, Yuji visits his dying grandfather at the hospital. On his deathbed, his grandfather tells Yuji to always help others and to die surrounded by people, not alone. Soon after, his grandfather passes away.<br><br>Back at school, Yuji finds his two club‑mates have broken the seal on Sukuna’s finger, curious about its power. Removing the seal draws multiple dangerous curses that begin to hunt them inside the old school building.<br><br>Trapped and helpless, Sasaki and Iguchi are about to be killed. To protect them, Yuji grabs the rotten cursed finger and swallows it down his throat.<br><br>Sukuna’s consciousness awakens and briefly takes over Yuji’s body, showing his demonic form. Unexpectedly, Yuji manages to regain full control and suppress Sukuna, something no‑one thought possible.<br><br>Megumi arrives ready to kill Yuji, believing the vessel will be consumed. He is shocked to see Yuji still fully himself. Megumi contacts his teacher, Satoru Gojo, to report the strange situation.<br><br>Gojo explains that Yuji can act as a living vessel. The plan: Yuji will travel to Jujutsu High, seek out and consume all remaining Sukuna fingers, then be executed once every finger is absorbed to eliminate the curse forever.<br><br>With heavy new purpose, Yuji accepts the dangerous path ahead of him.",
